  "step_2": "The individual reports considering the possibility of avoiding a loss in Lottery A (50% chance of losing nothing) versus the certainty of losing 500 Euros in Lottery B. The individual explicitly contrasts the hope of avoiding loss (in A) with the definite knowledge of loss (in B), and states that 'hope' won over certainty. The justification centers on the psychological appeal of avoiding a sure loss, emphasizing emotional reasoning ('die Hoffnung hat bei mir gesiegt') rather than a structural analysis of the lotteries. The individual focuses on the presence of certainty in B and the presence of uncertainty (and hope) in A.",
